**Summary**
- `src/styles/tokens.css`: added `--text-scale: 1` default (in the global `:root` block, theme-agnostic) and wrapped all 10 `--fs-*` tokens (`xs/sm/base/md/lg/xl/2xl/3xl/4xl/5xl`) in `calc(<px> * var(--text-scale))`. Existing `var(--fs-md)` consumers unchanged.
- `src/components/SettingsMenu.tsx`: exported `TEXT_SCALE_STORAGE_KEY = 'aiLecturer.textScale'`, `readTextScale()` (clamp + `Number.isFinite` guard), `applyTextScale()` (writes `--text-scale` inline on `<html>`). New `textScale` state, `onTextScaleSelect` mirroring `onFontSelect`, and a new `<TextScaleGroup>` rendered below Font with `data-testid="settings-text-scale-slider"` / `data-testid="settings-text-scale-value"`.
- `src/app/layout.tsx`: boot script now also reads `aiLecturer.textScale`, parses+clamps to [0.8, 1.4], and writes `--text-scale` inline before first paint — no flash on reload.
- Quality: `tsc --noEmit` clean; `vitest run` 680/680 pass.
- Browser-verified at 1280px: baseline h1 22px → slider→1.4 raises to 30.8px, persists across reload at `domcontentloaded` (proving boot-script applies pre-paint), slider→1.0 restores. Screenshots at `/tmp/us-130-{1-baseline,2-scale-1.4,3-after-reload,4-back-to-1}.png`.
